  {
   "id": "poole/MRK.14",
   "range": "MRK.14",
   "kind": "chapter",
   "hash": "73e8ddf2",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p1-0e2589f1",
     "text": "Mar 14:1,2 The chief priests and scribes conspire against Christ.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:1",
       "ref": "MRK.14.1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p2-fa79f98c",
     "text": "Mar 14:3-9 A woman pours precious ointment on his head.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:3-9",
       "ref": "MRK.14.3-9"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p3-0d1bafb5",
     "text": "Mar 14:10,11 Judas covenants to betray him,",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:10",
       "ref": "MRK.14.10"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p4-c1b95c2f",
     "text": "Mar 14:12-21 Christ eats the passover, and showeth that one of his disciples should betray him.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:12-21",
       "ref": "MRK.14.12-21"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p5-68b00002",
     "text": "Mar 14:22-26 He institutes his last supper,",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:22-26",
       "ref": "MRK.14.22-26"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p6-4766ca8e",
     "text": "Mar 14:27-31 foretells the desertion of all his disciples, and Peter’s denial of him.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:27-31",
       "ref": "MRK.14.27-31"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p7-9acc4d06",
     "text": "Mar 14:32-42 His agony and prayer in the garden.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:32-42",
       "ref": "MRK.14.32-42"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p8-055bdf45",
     "text": "Mar 14:43-52 He is betrayed by Judas, and apprehended: his disciples flee.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:43-52",
       "ref": "MRK.14.43-52"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p9-523350c7",
     "text": "Mar 14:53-65 He is carried before the council, falsely accused, examined, pronounced guilty and treated with indignity.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:53-65",
       "ref": "MRK.14.53-65"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14#p10-1c701871",
     "text": "Mar 14:66-72 Peter’s denial, and repentance.",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mar 14:66-72",
       "ref": "MRK.14.66-72"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "poole/MRK.14.1",
   "range": "MRK.14.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "51da3642",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "poole/MRK.14.1#p1-36ead12a",
     "text": "Ver. 1,2. Matthew saith the same, only he bringeth it in as said to the disciples by Christ. This must be said upon that day in the week which we call Tuesday, for Friday was the passover day, when began the feast of unleavened bread."
    },
    {
